From 47b994ef12a5ce6f7a47ab8921092bfd537d13a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Micha=C5=82=20Iwanicki?= <michal.iwanicki@3mdeb.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 17:22:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] tpmlib: store the last byte of a TIS response at the end of
 the buffer
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

tis_recv() reads all but the last byte of the response body into the
buffer and then reads the last byte into the first byte of that same
body, so the final byte of every response is whatever the buffer held
before. A PCR read on the MZ33-AR1 returned digests whose last byte was
zero for that reason. The last byte now lands after the bytes already
received.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Michał Iwanicki <michal.iwanicki@3mdeb.com>
---
 tpmlib/tis.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tpmlib/tis.c b/tpmlib/tis.c
index a8e5b00..fb5bcf6 100644
--- a/tpmlib/tis.c
+++ b/tpmlib/tis.c
@@ -212,8 +212,8 @@ size_t tis_recv(enum tpm_family f, struct tpmbuff *buf)
 	if (!tis_data_available(locality))
 		return 0;
 
-	/* read last byte */
-	if (recv_data(buf_ptr, 1) != 1)
+	/* read last byte into its own slot after the bytes already received */
+	if (recv_data(buf_ptr + expected - 1, 1) != 1)
 		return 0;
 
 	/* make sure we read everything */
-- 
2.55.0

